 * display_name and is_verified) on a member profile and ensures those changes
 * are correctly persisted and returned. It also checks that non-editable fields
 * (id, email, registration timestamp, etc.) remain unchanged after the update.
 * Only permitted fields, as defined by the IUpdate DTO, are modified.
 *
 * Steps:
 *
 * 1. Register a new member and record their profile fields.
 * 2. As admin, update allowed fields (display_name, is_verified) using the admin
 *    endpoint.
 * 3. Assert that the returned member reflects all updated fields, while restricted
 *    fields are unchanged.
 */
export async function test_api_discussionBoard_test_update_member_profile_as_admin_success(
  connection: api.IConnection,
) {
  // 1. Create a new member to be updated.
  const memberCreateInput: IDiscussionBoardMember.ICreate = {
    display_name: RandomGenerator.name(),
    email: typia.random<string & tags.Format<"email">>(),
